BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pawsitively Pets: Hands-on Animal Education
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260817T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260817T160000
UID:69c58b3b2866a5b48844a10c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Pawsitively Pets is a hands-on animal education program for ch
 ildren of all ages. Our wonderful animal team is made up of an assortment 
 of rescued pets that have found their forever home with us. Our goal is to
  provide our animal team with a permanent home and the best possible care\
 , while sharing our love or animals with others. All programs focus on res
 ponsible pet ownership\, and the life-long commitment of owning a pet.\nPl
 ease note this program is suitable for children 5 years old up with adult 
 accompaniment. This program is meant for children to attend with their ad
 ults or caregiver.\nWhen signing up please indicate how many CHILDREN are 
 attending\n. One adult may attend per child\, but the adult does not nee
 d to register.\nThis program can hold up to 25 children.\nInformation Coll
 ection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the 
 Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 2
 0(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program 
 registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library ha
 ndles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@
 tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Gerrard/Ashdale\, The program will be held on the second floor in
  the program room.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c58b3b2866a5b48844a10c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
