BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wonder Workshop: Community Challenge
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260810T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260810T153000
UID:6a1063d7c6a1dc3d00d5656b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:What do you see when you walk through your community? Have you
  ever thought about building something for your community that would have 
 a positive impact on the people living there?\nPut on your thinking cap an
 d use your imagination to design and build something that would make your 
 community stronger!\nPlus\, enter a prize draw for a chance to win an awes
 ome book.\nThis is a workshop for kids ages 4 to 8 !\nSpace is limited. R
 egistration is required. Registration will begin on Monday\, July 20\, at 
 9AM.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this for
 m is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Ac
 t\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used 
 for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions ab
 out how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline
  staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto
  ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Morningside\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a1063d7c6a1dc3d00d5656b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
